{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794736712,"nonce":"yLqpoXMkKfQJem8h/uHBRcpncWs=","message":"P0 audit, part 1: where the hook runs and what the TAST file lacks (Haxe 4.3.6, filters.ml, finalization.ml, genhl.ml).\n\nCorrection to the first comment: `Context.onGenerate` runs BEFORE DCE, not after. `Filters.run` runs the before_save callbacks, then `destruction` (type filters, DCE, post-DCE type filters), then after_filters. Counts on a small program are identical under -dce full, std and no (103 classes, 1071 functions, 27614 nodes). The 28959 -\u003e 27447 node drop in the first comment came from the expression filters.\n\nAfter the type filters the program differs from the onGenerate one: DCE removes classes and fields, add_field_inits moves field initializers into constructors, apply_native_paths renames, add_rtti, patch_constructors and remove_extern_fields run. genhl compiles that program. The plugin now has `exportFinal` and `countFinal`, which register on `callbacks#add_after_filters` (08cf515e). The Haxe exporter cannot reach that hook, so it stays the oracle for the onGenerate export only.\n\nUnit suite (compile-hl.hxml, -dce full), native count:\n- onGenerate: 2609 classes, 10215 functions, 753 variable initializers, 298670 nodes.\n- after filters: 2080 classes, 8812 functions, 163 variable initializers, 276248 nodes. The file is 9.9 MB against 10.7 MB, and tast_dump reports it valid.\n- hello-size program: 1071 -\u003e 398 functions, 27614 -\u003e 13613 nodes.\n\nThe lowering should read the after-filters export, so it does not reimplement DCE, add_field_inits, native paths or RTTI.\n\nGaps in the file, found so far:\n1. `cl_init` (static `__init__` blocks) is exported by neither writer. Math, haxe.Resource, hl.UI and hl.Profile have one.\n2. Type order. `Finalization.sort_types` orders `com.types` so a class comes after its superclass, interfaces, and anything its static initializers and constructors reference. genhl's start-up function runs every cl_init in that order, then the static variable initializers in that order, then main. Both writers sort types by kind and path, which discards it. Needs an order field on class records, or a list.\n3. Metadata. The file has none. genhl reads @:hlNative (class and field, with library, name or version), @:struct (a class lowers to HStruct, not HObj), @:packed on fields, @:coreType on abstracts, @:realPath, @:noExpr, and `Texpr.build_metadata` for runtime @:meta (reflection).\n4. The filters before the hook are already applied, so the file holds their output: ForRemap (no TFor), abstract casts, local statics, inline constructors, the Exceptions filter, captured_vars. HL uses `pf_capture_policy = CPWrapRef` and `pf_pad_nulls = true`.\n\nNext: the genhl type mapping, cast matrix and expression arms, then a table of constructs against what AIR has.","files":null}]}